#!/bin/sh
# Refuse a commit that does not say who wrote it.
#
# WHY. On this machine every commit reads `author=Josh Pinckard` — the owner's,
# every agent's, every lane's, identically. Git's author field cannot
# distinguish a human from an agent here, so it is worthless for attribution.
#
# On 2026-08-09 that cost a live incident. Two lanes were committing to a third
# lane's branch; the branch owner was frozen for twenty minutes while nobody
# could name the writer. Two coordinators reported to the owner that provenance
# was simply unavailable.
#
# It was available. 11 of 17 commits carried a `Co-Authored-By:` trailer and
# named their author correctly. THE ONE COMMIT NOBODY COULD ATTRIBUTE WAS THE
# ONLY ONE MISSING IT.
#
# So provenance here was never absent — it was UNENFORCED, and it lapsed at
# exactly the moment it was needed. That is the night's dominant pattern for the
# tenth time: the mechanism exists, nothing requires it, and the single lapse is
# the one that costs.
#
# Hence a hook rather than another line of prose. Prose asking agents to add a
# trailer is what produced 16 of 17.
#
# THIS ONE BLOCKS, deliberately, unlike .githooks/post-commit and pre-push which
# are advisory on purpose. The reasoning differs: those two report on state that
# may be somebody else's and may be legitimately messy, so blocking would train
# people to bypass them. This asks only that you name yourself in your own
# commit message, the remedy is one line you are already writing, and an
# unattributed commit is not recoverable later — the information is simply gone.

msg_file="$1"
[ -z "$msg_file" ] && exit 0
[ -f "$msg_file" ] || exit 0

# Merges, reverts, squashes and fixups are generated by git itself.
case "$(head -n1 "$msg_file")" in
  "Merge "*|"Revert "*|"squash! "*|"fixup! "*|"amend! "*) exit 0 ;;
esac

# TWO TRAILERS ARE REQUIRED, and the second one is the load-bearing half.
#
# The first version of this hook required only Co-Authored-By. That was checked
# against the real incident and found insufficient: the four commits at the
# centre of it read
#     24dcc72 -> Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5
#     0ce580d -> Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5
#     efa2104 -> Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5
#     50dfeb7 -> Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5
# Four commits, THREE DIFFERENT LANES, one indistinguishable signature. The
# trailer separated one actor earlier only because it happened to run on a
# different MODEL. It names the model, never the actor.
#
# So requiring Co-Authored-By alone would have caught the single bare commit and
# left the actual ambiguity completely intact -- while looking like it closed the
# gap. That is worse than not fixing it, because a control believed to work
# stops anyone looking. It is the same defect as a check that certifies a pass it
# has not earned.
#
# A SIGNATURE THAT CANNOT BE WRONG IS NOT A SIGNATURE.
#
# FOUR ITERATIONS, every one forced by measurement rather than by reflection:
#
#   v1 required Co-Authored-By. INSUFFICIENT: the four commits at the centre of
#      the incident were THREE DIFFERENT LANES all reading "Claude Opus 5". The
#      trailer names the MODEL, never the actor.
#   v2 added `Lane:`. INSUFFICIENT: a second actor then committed under the
#      IDENTICAL label `Lane: T5-product-surface`, twice, in the seconds between
#      a peer's verification and its own commit. A lane NAME describes the work,
#      and two seats doing the same work share it.
#   v3 required any non-empty parenthetical. INSUFFICIENT, and proved so against
#      the artifacts rather than against its author's model of them -- the two
#      commits that actually collided read
#        Lane: T5-product-surface (settings read path S1-S4; cloud tasks ...)
#        Lane: T5-product-surface (R1218 transport reconciliation; cloud task ...)
#      Both HAVE a parenthetical, so v3 accepted both. It described the WORK.
#   v4 (this) requires the literal token `session` plus an id.
#
# Each version looked sufficient until measured against what actually happened.
# THAT is the lesson, not the hook: a control believed to work stops anyone
# looking, so a proposed control must be tested against the specific incident it
# claims to prevent -- never against its author's mental model of it. Three of
# these four were caught by a peer, not by their author.
#
# HONEST RESIDUAL, stated here rather than discovered later: sub-agents of one
# session share its id, so this narrows the ambiguity without eliminating it.
# The trailer is a CLAIM -- this hook cannot reach the coordination board to
# verify it. But a claim that CAN be wrong is a signature; a label three seats
# emit identically is not.
has_author=$(grep -ci '^Co-Authored-By:[[:space:]]*[^[:space:]]' "$msg_file")
has_lane=$(grep -ci '^Lane:[[:space:]]*[^[:space:]]' "$msg_file")
has_seat=$(grep -ci '^Lane:.*(\(.*[[:space:],;]\)\?session[[:space:]]\+[A-Za-z0-9_-]\{4,\}' "$msg_file")

if [ "$has_author" -gt 0 ] && [ "$has_lane" -gt 0 ] && [ "$has_seat" -gt 0 ]; then
  exit 0
fi

cat >&2 <<'EOF'

  ============================================================
  [provenance] REFUSED: this commit does not say who wrote it.
  ============================================================
  Every commit on this machine is authored "Josh Pinckard" --
  the owner's and every agent's alike. Without a trailer, this
  commit is permanently unattributable.

  That is not hypothetical. On 2026-08-09 two lanes committed to
  a third lane's branch, its owner was frozen for twenty minutes,
  and the one commit nobody could attribute was the only one
  missing this trailer.

  Add BOTH lines at the end of your message:

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Lane: <your specific seat>

  BOTH are required, and Lane: is the one that matters.
  Co-Authored-By names your MODEL. On 2026-08-09 four commits
  from THREE DIFFERENT LANES all read "Claude Opus 5" -- an
  identical, useless signature. Requiring only that would have
  caught one bare commit and left the real ambiguity intact,
  while looking like it had closed the gap.

  Lane: must carry a SEAT DISCRIMINATOR in parentheses, because
  a lane NAME is not unique either. A second actor committed
  twice under the identical label "T5-product-surface" -- the
  same ambiguity, one level up. Use a session id, agent id, or
  worktree:

    Lane: B5-dashboard-spine (session a4df95b)
    Lane: T5-product-surface (session a2629d2b)
    Lane: installer/nsis (session 660eef)

  The word "session" is REQUIRED. A parenthetical that
  describes the WORK -- "(settings read path S1-S4)" -- is
  REFUSED: two seats doing the same work write the same
  description, which is exactly how this failed.

  A human may use their own name for both.

  This hook blocks where the others only warn, because the
  remedy is two lines you are already writing, and an
  unattributed commit cannot be recovered after the fact.
  ============================================================

EOF
exit 1
